<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan Rafael Mora Porras</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1814">1814</a>–<a href="/years/1860">1860</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan Rafael Mora Porras was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> merchant and president of Costa Rica from 1849 to 1859. He led the Central American coalition that defeated the American filibuster <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-walker">William Walker</a> in Nicaragua in 1856 and 1857, and is honoured as a national hero. Overthrown in 1859, he was executed after a failed attempt to return to power in 1860.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-rafael-mora-porras.jpg" alt="Juan Rafael Mora Porras" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aquiles Bigot · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juan_Rafael_Mora_Porras.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
